  "id": "f7e705e01dfe",
  "title": "Lions' Commentary on Unix: Why It Was Secretly Copied for 20 Years",
  "originalTitle": "Lions' Commentary on Unix: Why It Was Secretly Copied for 20 Years",
  "source": "Hacker News",
  "category": "Tech",
  "url": "https://fosscomics.com/posts/17.%20Lions%27%20Commentary%20on%20Unix/",
  "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T05:12:59.000Z",
  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div> <article> <div> <p>Posted on Nov 25, 2026</p> <nav aria-label=\"Languages\"><a href=\"https://fosscomics.com/posts/17.%20Lions'%20Commentary%20on%20Unix/\" lang=\"en\" hreflang=\"en\" aria-label=\"English\" aria-current=\"page\">EN</a><a href=\"https://fosscomics.com/ko/posts/17.%20Lions'%20Commentary%20on%20Unix/\" lang=\"ko\" hreflang=\"ko\" aria-label=\"한국어\">KO</a></nav> </div> <section id=\"comic-transcript\"> <section id=\"comic-panel-teaching-operating-systems\">\n<p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Lions\">John Lions</a> was teaching <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operating_system\">operating systems</a> at the University of New South Wales in Australia.</p> <!-- dialogue: lions-teaching-question -->\n<div><blockquote><p>What's the best way to<br>teach operating systems?</p></blockquote></div><!-- /dialogue -->\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"comic-panel-writing-a-textbook\"> <!-- dialogue: lions-source-difficulty -->\n<div><blockquote><p>They need to study the Unix source.<br>But it's tough going.</p></blockquote></div><!-- /dialogue -->\n\n<!-- dialogue: lions-write-textbook -->\n<div><blockquote><p>I'll write my<br>own textbook.</p></blockquote></div><!-- /dialogue -->\n\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"comic-panel-restricting-source-code\">\n<p>Early on, Unix source could be studied in class. But at USENIX in June 1979, AT&amp;T announced new Version 7 license terms restricting courses that disclosed or discussed source code. Distribution of Lions' book was tightly controlled as well [5][6].</p> <!-- dialogue: empire-stop-source -->\n<div><blockquote><p>I am altering the license.<br>Pray I don't alter it<br>any further.</p></blockquote></div><!-- /dialogue -->\n\n</section>\n<div id=\"comic-panel-forbidding-other-systems\"><blockquote><p>There is no escape<br>from our operating system.</p></blockquote></div>\n<section id=\"comic-panel-raiding-the-classroom\"> <div> </div> <div><blockquote><p>He's teaching from the Unix source code!<br>Seize the books!<br>Run!</p></blockquote></div></section> <div id=\"comic-panel-firing-at-the-reader\"> </div>\n<div id=\"comic-panel-reader-is-hit\"> </div>\n<div>\n<div id=\"comic-panel-mocking-the-reader\"><blockquote><p>I find your interest<br>in source code disturbing.</p></blockquote></div>\n<div id=\"comic-panel-stepping-on-the-book\"><blockquote><p>Just use the system calls.<br>Learn a little theory.<br>Leave the internals to us.</p></blockquote></div>\n</div>\n<section id=\"comic-panel-studying-the-source\"> <!-- dialogue: student-needs-source -->\n<div><blockquote><p>Theory isn't enough.<br>I need to see the code.</p></blockquote></div><!-- /dialogue -->\n\n<!-- dialogue: student-only-source -->\n<div><blockquote><p>This code is our only hope<br>of understanding an OS.</p></blockquote></div><!-- /dialogue -->\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"comic-panel-learning-from-copies\">\n<p>For roughly twenty years before the official edition appeared, computer-science students studied from unauthorized photocopies. The book helped a generation of students learn to build operating systems of their own [5][8].</p> <div> </div> </section>\n\n<section id=\"comic-panel-published-book-cover\"> <div> </div> <p>You can read a reconstructed version of the commentary as a <a href=\"http://www.lemis.com/grog/Documentation/Lions/book.pdf\">PDF</a>, or order a print copy on <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lions-Commentary-Unix-John/dp/1573980137/\">Amazon</a>. The Unix Version 6 source code is available separately from <a href=\"https://www.tuhs.org/Archive/Distributions/Research/Dennis_v6/\">TUHS</a>.</p></section>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lions%27_Commentary_on_UNIX_6th_Edition,_with_Source_Code\">Lions' Commentary on UNIX 6th Edition, with Source Code</a></li>\n<li>John Lions, <em>Lions' Commentary on UNIX 6th Edition, with Source Code</em>, Peer-to-Peer Communications, 1996 (ISBN 1-57398-013-7).</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/System_call\">System call</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://archive.org/details/unix_news_march-1977/page/n3/mode/2up\">UNIX News, Vol. 2 No. 3, March 1977</a> - John Lions's March 11, 1977 letter and the announcement of book distribution to Unix licensees.</li>\n<li>Rachel Chalmers, <a href=\"https://www.salon.com/1999/11/30/lions_2/\">\"Code critic\"</a>, <em>Salon</em>, November 30, 1999 - recollections from students and Dennis Ritchie, distribution restrictions, and the path to publication.</li>\n<li>Peter H. Salus, <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20100505072836/http://www.groklaw.net/article.php?story=20050502114023686\"><em>The Daemon, the GNU and the Penguin</em>, Chapter 6: \"1979\"</a>, 2005 - the Version 7 license terms announced at USENIX in June 1979 and restrictions on classroom use.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/DoctorWkt/IEEE_Milestone_Lions_Commentary/blob/main/Emails/dmr_to_wkt_1995_10_22.txt\">Dennis Ritchie's October 22, 1995 letter</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/DoctorWkt/IEEE_Milestone_Lions_Commentary/blob/main/Emails/salus_to_wkt_1996_06_12.txt\">Peter H. Salus's July 12, 1996 letter</a> - publication-permission correspondence preserved by Warren Toomey.</li>\n<li>MIT, <a href=\"https://pdos.csail.mit.edu/6.828/2017/xv6.html\">\"Xv6, a simple Unix-like teaching operating system\"</a>, \"History and Background\" - teaching with Lions's commentary and the background to xv6.</li>\n</ol>\n<!-- text-overlay-font-licenses\nCopyright 2023 The Playpen Sans Project Authors (https://github.com/TypeTogether/Playpen-Sans)\n\nThis Font Software is licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1.\nThis license is copied below, and is also available with a FAQ at:\nhttps://openfontlicense.org -&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-&#45;-